  "explanation": "Over an Ab bass, Bb11/Ab and Abmaj13#11 share six notes: Ab Bb C D Eb F. The Lydian chord adds one more, G.",
  "why": "G is the major 7th of Ab. With it the chord floats and can stay; without it the chord belongs to Bb and leans toward Eb.",
